//
// What the binary is allowed to say about itself. Every value here is captured
// when the platform is *configured*, so `--version` names the build that
// produced a result rather than the tree as it stands when someone asks.
//
// The VP++ patch series is emitted as a table rather than passed as a compile
// definition because its records contain `;`, which is CMake's list separator:
// a `-D` would split each record mid-field and the binary would report a
// mangled provenance. Provenance that is subtly wrong is worse than absent.

